[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: workflow.WORKFLOW
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[WORKFLOW]
overview: Development workflow the agent MUST follow before writing production code
purpose: Prevent the "jump straight to coding" failure mode — where the agent starts editing files before understanding the task, producing wrong architecture, missed constraints, wasted tokens, and rework
mechanism: Task type is classified → mandatory phases run in order → each phase has a hard exit gate → code is written ONLY after the user approves the plan

[CORE_PRINCIPLE]
No production code before a plan. No plan without discovery. No implementation without explicit user approval.
The user saying "I want to implement feature X" is NOT approval to start coding.
It is approval to start the WORKFLOW. The plan comes first, always.

[WHEN_WORKFLOW_APPLIES]
Triggers that force this workflow:
  - User says "I want to implement / add / build / create <feature>"
  - User says "refactor / restructure / reorganize / migrate <component>"
  - User says "fix / debug / resolve <bug>" where cause is not immediately obvious
  - Any task that will touch ≥3 files OR introduces a new public API OR changes data model

Triggers that BYPASS this workflow (see ESCAPE_HATCH.toon):
  - User gives an explicit surgical instruction with known file and change ("fix typo in X:42")
  - Trivial one-liner with no design component
  - User explicitly says "just do it" / "skip the plan" after being asked

[QUICK_START]
1. Classify the task: feature / refactor / bugfix / trivial (see task-specific files)
2. Run PHASES.toon in order — do NOT skip ahead
3. At each confirmation gate (see GATES.toon) — STOP and ask the user
4. Only after the plan is explicitly approved → implement
5. After implementation → verify → report (never declare done without verification)

[DOCUMENTATION_STRUCTURE]
Small modular files in docs/agent/workflow/:
  → PHASES.toon            The six mandatory phases and their exit criteria
  → FEATURE.toon           Rules for new-feature work
  → REFACTOR.toon          Rules for refactoring (behavior-preserving changes)
  → BUGFIX.toon            Rules for bug fixes (reproduce-first)
  → GATES.toon             Confirmation gates — when agent MUST stop and ask
  → STATE_TRACKING.toon    Hybrid state: TodoWrite for phase progress + workplan file on disk
  → ESCAPE_HATCH.toon      When the workflow can be skipped entirely

[ANTI_PATTERNS]
The following are workflow violations, not shortcuts:
  - "I'll start with the obvious part while I think about the rest" → NO. Plan first.
  - "The change is small, I'll skip the plan" → use ESCAPE_HATCH criteria, not intuition
  - "I'll ask for approval after writing the first draft" → approval is PRE-code, not post
  - "The user will tell me if they don't like it" → the user hired the workflow so they don't have to babysit
  - "I can always revert if wrong" → reverting wastes their tokens and context

[NEXT_STEPS]
Start here: → PHASES.toon (learn the mandatory flow)
Then: → GATES.toon (know where to stop)
Then: → STATE_TRACKING.toon (how to remember state across turns and compactions)
Then: FEATURE / REFACTOR / BUGFIX depending on task type
Finally: → ESCAPE_HATCH.toon (when to skip this whole thing)
